If inauspicious → check ternary: 
  Past: has this modification pattern succeeded before?
  Present: is the build currently passing?
  Future: will this change enable or disable future capabilities?
If 2/3 ternary gates approve → proceed with warning, not block.
This aligns with your trauma-informed design: DOC survival required bending rules when all three survival metrics (past experience, present resources, future viability) aligned.
Test 2: assimilateHiveEvent() — Cognitive Immunology as Palindrome
